questions.question_text:
The graph below shows the cost $C$ and revenue $R$ for selling $n$ floral bouquets.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.9]
\draw[gray!30,very thin] (0,0) grid (8,8);
\draw[-{Stealth},thick] (0,0) -- (8.6,0);
\draw[-{Stealth},thick] (0,0) -- (0,8.6);
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (1,-0.15) {$10$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2,-0.15) {$20$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3,-0.15) {$30$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (4,-0.15) {$40$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (5,-0.15) {$50$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (6,-0.15) {$60$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (7,-0.15) {$70$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (8,-0.15) {$80$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,1) {$100$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,2) {$200$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,3) {$300$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,4) {$400$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,5) {$500$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,6) {$600$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,7) {$700$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,8) {$800$};
\node[below,font=\small] at (4.3,-0.9) {Number of units ($n$)};
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-1.3,4.3) {Dollars (\$)};
\draw[thick,blue] (0,2) -- (8,6) node[pos=0.35,above left,font=\small] {$C = 200 + 5n$};
\draw[thick,red] (0,0) -- (8,8) node[pos=0.95,below right,font=\small] {$R = 10n$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which point represents the break-even point?

